keanu reeves no longer really retired  assassin has killed hundreds of  opponents when they screwed him over or  got in his way there's no stopping baba  yaga here are some of the hardest to  watch most memorably brutal deaths in  the john wick series thus far  this is the death that set john wick off  on his killing spree and any animal  lover can likely relate to such an urge  underneath all the glorious violence and  destruction this franchise is ultimately  an ode to man's best friends dogs and  cars director chad stahlski profess a  love of dogs to up rocks in 2019 saying  his began as a child in a household that  raised irish wolfhounds strahelski's  background inspired him to incorporate  dogs into the john wick films we see  this first with the adorable baby beagle  gifted to wick posthumously by his  recently deceased wife helen her passing  sets the stage for the first film and  knowing her time was near she scheduled  daisy's arrival for when jon would need  her most the puppy acts as an anchor for  the grieving husband giving him a reason  to keep going each day tragically his  tentative grip on becoming whole slips  away when russian thugs break into his  house kill daisy and steal his prized 69  mustang a wedding gift from helen it's  heartbreaking to see the little puppy  die so much so that even the actor  tasked with killing the puppy on set  felt the need to cuddle daisy between  takes he can't blame jon for hunting  down every person affiliated with  killing that innocent puppy and stealing  his car but thankfully in real life the  beagle is alive and well and has been  living with a loving family who have  since renamed him wick  wick committed the ultimate unforgivable  sin in john wick chapter 2 when he  killed santino d'antonio on the neutral  ground of the continental this set every  bounty hunter in the city after wick who  attempted to lose them in chapter 3  parabellum by hiding out in a central  park horse stable in one of his most  creative and brutal moves wick used one  of the horses and the stables as a  weapon to fend off his pursuers placing  the horse between himself and one of the  assassins rick encouraged the horse to  back kick his opponent in the sternum he  then slapped the horse's thigh so it  followed with a double bag kick to the  guy's jaw who instantly dropped like a  sack of potatoes then wick wrapped the  horse's reins around his last living  opponent's neck dragging him from the  stable behind him it's pretty intense  and not a position anyone would ever  want to be in  after escaping from the stable on his  death horse and parabellum wick is  pursued by motorcyclist gangsters  through downtown manhattan in the  process wick executes some amazing trick  riding and manages to vanquish all those  in pursuit the motorcyclists get shot in  the face and crash into other cars  pretty hard amazingly keanu reeves  performed the stunt riding in the scene  skills he originally acquired while  shooting the 2013 action and fantasy  film 47 ronin in order to keep reeves  safe while filming the scene the crew  set up a custom wire harness to act as a  safety net in case he fell or the horse  took off unexpectedly even with the  safety harness reeves had some close  calls which required him to quickly pull  his feet out to the stirrups and quote  make himself small so as to not hit  anything it sounds like reeves job  sometimes is almost as dangerous as that  of john wick in an ironic twist the  russian thurgood orchestrated breaking  into john's house was the son of russian  crime boss vigo tarasov as we learned in  the original film wick and taurus off of  former associates when he was still an  assassin before wick quit his life of  crime and killing to settle down and  marry helen so after vigo learns what  his son has done he warns joseph about  wix's quote focus commitment and sheer  will comparing him to the russian  boogeyman we call him  to give his heedless son an idea of how  dangerous wick is viggo tells joseph  about how he once killed three men in a  bar using only a pencil this story is  later repeated by vigo's brother in  chapter two but stahelski wasn't content  to just let his audience hear about this  mind-boggling feat later in chapter 2  wick would bring the legend to life by  recreating it while escaping assassins  in new york cornered by two men in a  small cafe area and bleeding badly the  scene has wick managing to deflect one  assassin's gunshot or grabbing for a  pencil lying by a service notepad then  he stabs one assailant in the chest with  the writing implement he uses a second  pencil to vanquish the other assassin  and finish off the first the stabs are  in places quite undelightful to watch  eliciting squeamish squeals from many a  viewer it can't help but make you look  at office supplies in a whole new  twisted light  in parabellum john wick adds to the list  of random inanimate objects he uses to  kill people when he executes a fellow  assassin using only a book in the new  york public library you would think a  library would provide a safe haven to  read but even there wit can find no  peace boban yamanovich of the dallas  mavericks plays his towering opponent  ernest he corners wig down one of the  abandoned isles and uses his long limbs  to his advantage to make matters worse  mayanovich's character has a knife and  manages to strike true stabbing wick in  the shoulder after a few deflected shots  then he grabs wick and kicks him down  the aisles while loudly and ironically  whispering for him to be quiet  the tide's turn for wick when he manages  to grab a particularly thick tome and  hits ernest squarely in the crotch  throat and face with it wick follows  with a crushing death blow by plating  the book on a tabletop smashing ernest's  face into the spine he bends his neck  and jaw back in horrific angles  accompanied by a sickening crack  perhaps one of the wildest sequences in  the john wick film takes place in  parabellum while on the run from ninjas  wick makes a stop inside an antique  weapons store to arm himself old west  style his foes follow him inside and  they all begin volleying knives at one  another like nerf darts shattering  countless glass display cases and  mirrors in the process one of the ninjas  gets stabbed in the back by two knives  thrown by his comrade before being  stabbed in the groin and a few other  areas of the body by wick much more  stabbing follows culminating with one of  the last surviving ninjas getting slowly  shanked in the eye which is super  uncomfortable to watch to top it all off  wick finishes off the last ninja by  throwing a tomahawk into a skull from  across the room it may look like chaos  but this sequence was intricately  planned and took a massive amount of  effort to complete stahelski told  polygon the inspiration for the scene  came from the good the bad and the ugly  when the big bad two go into a gun shop  after hours for supplies after starting  with that spark of inspiration stahelski  expanded the scene to include an epic  knife fight akin to what he eloquently  described as a quote snowball fight only  far deadlier  many scenes in the john wick films use a  combination of cgi and practical effects  to create images that would otherwise be  impossible or incredibly dangerous to  perform without digital aid one such  example is an epic motorcycle chase  scene in parabellum when some of zero's  ninjas are chasing wake through brooklyn  the scene gets even spicier when the  ninjas pull out katanas and attempt to  slice and dice wick while they're all  riding around on two wheels wick manages  to turn their sword against them  skewering ninjas like sheesh kebabs who  then crash into each other in an  explosive domino effect despite the  hyper-realism of the scene the riders  hitting the pavement were all edited  into the scene with cgi layered into  shots with real actors a stride  motorcycle sled riggs mounted in front  of green screens the cringe-inducing  scenes go to show how great of a job the  visual effects team performed  burning to death sounds like one of the  most painful ways to face your final  moments even so those are the  consequences for being complicit in the  killing of john wick's dog and theft of  his car this fiery moment of vengeance  takes place in the original film when  wick finally locates joseph tarasov  thanks to his dad vigo sharing the  information with the determined assassin  it seems there's no honor among thieves  even when they're family wic tracks  joseph and his thugs to a safe house in  brooklyn which suddenly becomes no  longer safe and our thugs flee for their  cars in hopes of a quick escape however  wick remotely blows up their cars before  they can flee which explode in  spectacular fashion when did he have  time to plant bombs on multiple cars who  cares they go boom while keanu reeves  walks in slow motion and that's what  matters while trying to make one final  desperate escape rick shoots joseph in  the stomach before shooting him in the  head while he's in the process of  protesting that it was just a dog though  he actually got off easy compared to the  guys who caught fire from the car bombs  and the dog is never just a dog  john may not be able to bring his puppy  daisy back but at least he's able to  reunite with his car chapter 2 opens  with wick infiltrating the chop shop of  abram tarasov uncle and brother to the  late joseph and viggo respectively with  wix 69 mustang in his shop he fears the  buggy men will come for his car and  leave a path of collateral damage in his  wake abram fails an accomplice in on the  gritty details of wick's capabilities  and a serious predicament while tara  sarva's telling his story wick is right  outside working his way into the shop by  quietly taking out abram's guys one at a  time one of those guys is on a smoke  break when wick sneaks up behind him and  as tarasov's voice over plays on  describing wick's focus commitment and  cheer will wick shoves a cigarette down  the man's throat from the rear then  punches him in the gut and while  covering his mouth forces a smoldering  cigarette down the man's throat one can  only imagine how brutally that would  hurt after decades of folks complaining  that hollywood glamorized her smoking  here's one scene that would seem to  drive home another albeit rare danger  associated with nicotine addiction  wick continues his quest to get his car  back with his next most brutal kill  which follows shortly after choking our  brahms thug with his own cigarette the  vengeful assassin sneaks up behind the  next body he crosses past with at the  chop shop only this bad guy has made the  wise decision not to smoke so wig does  what he does best and improvises by  taking him down and choking him with a  wire it seems like a very slow painful  way to die especially compared to how  quickly a lot of the other deaths occur  in the film via more humane manners such  as point-blank gunshots this may seem  like a hard death to swallow but many  follow in john wick's bloody footsteps  at least he gets his car back even if he  does immediately trash it while making  his getaway it just goes to show with  the right level of focus commitment and  sheer will anything is possible even  killing hundreds of people in endlessly  creative and savage ways zahelsky told  the los angeles times in 2019 that he  and his stunt team got bored easily with  repetition so it will be interesting to  see how they keep all the killing  feeling novel in the upcoming films  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

